BT 1 0 0 1 0 49.5 Tm /F1 8 Tf 11.5 TL (Coronary Artery Disease \(CAD\) develops through the progressive accumulation of fibrofatty atheromatous plaques within the epicardial coronary) Tj T* (arteries. Over decades, this atherogenesis narrows the arterial lumen, creating a critical mismatch between myocardial oxygen demand and) Tj T* (coronary blood supply. While chronic stable angina manifests when luminal stenosis exceeds roughly 70% under physiological stress, plaque) Tj T* (rupture and subsequent thrombus formation can precipitate acute myocardial infarction \(AMI\) or fatal ventricular arrhythmias even in arteries with) Tj T* (hemodynamically moderate \(50\22670%\) baseline narrowing.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
