q
.176471 .215686 .282353 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 49.5 Tm /F1 8 Tf 11.5 TL (Historically, the definitive reference standard for diagnosing coronary stenosis has been invasive coronary angiography \(cardiac catheterization\).) Tj T* -0.095 Tw (However, catheterization is invasive, costly, requires specialized hospital catheterization suites, and carries non-negligible procedural risks \(such as) Tj T* 0 Tw (arterial dissection, stroke, contrast nephropathy, and life-threatening ventricular fibrillation\). Consequently, modern cardiology relies on) Tj T* (non-invasive pre-test probability stratification using physiological biomarkers\227such as resting 12-lead electrocardiography, treadmill exercise) Tj T* (tolerance, echocardiographic fluoroscopy, and nuclear myocardial perfusion scintigraphy\227to identify patients requiring urgent catheterization.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
