BT 1 0 0 1 0 49.5 Tm 11.5 TL /F1 8 Tf .176471 .215686 .282353 rg (1. ) Tj /F2 8 Tf (The Catastrophic Cost of a False Negative \(Type II Error\):) Tj /F1 8 Tf ( A patient harboring angiographically significant coronary stenosis is classified by) Tj T* (the model as disease-free \($y=1 \\rightarrow \\hat{y}=0$\). Reassured by the erroneous prediction, the patient is discharged without) Tj T* (guideline-directed medical therapy \(such as high-intensity statins, ACE inhibitors, or dual antiplatelet therapy\) and without anatomical) Tj T* (revascularization. Within weeks or months, plaque rupture triggers unheralded transmural myocardial infarction or sudden cardiac death. The) Tj T* (clinical outcome is catastrophic, irreversible, and potentially fatal.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 46 416 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 38 Tm 11.5 TL /F1 8 Tf .176471 .215686 .282353 rg (2. ) Tj /F2 8 Tf (The Manageable Cost of a False Positive \(Type I Error\):) Tj /F1 8 Tf ( A healthy individual is predicted to have coronary disease \($y=0 \\rightarrow) Tj T* (\\hat{y}=1$\). The patient is referred for secondary non-invasive testing \(such as stress echocardiography or CT coronary angiography\) or diagnostic) Tj T* (catheterization, accompanied by transient patient anxiety. The clinical consequence is monetary and administrative; patient survival is never) Tj T* (jeopardized.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 46 387 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 15 Tm 11.5 TL /F1 8 Tf .176471 .215686 .282353 rg (To reflect this clinical reality, our model optimization protocol explicitly prioritized ) Tj /F2 8 Tf (Sensitivity \(Recall\)) Tj /F1 8 Tf ( and ) Tj /F2 8 Tf (ROC-AUC) Tj /F1 8 Tf ( over raw overall accuracy.) Tj T* (The objective was to minimize the False Negative Rate below 12% while maintaining adequate clinical specificity.) Tj T* ET
