BT 1 0 0 1 0 130 Tm 11.5 TL /F1 8 Tf .176471 .215686 .282353 rg (To contextualize where machine learning fits into modern cardiology, it is instructive to compare algorithmic models against traditional clinical risk) Tj T* (scoring paradigms:) Tj  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 8 Tf (The Framingham Risk Score:) Tj /F1 8 Tf ( Pioneered in 1998, Framingham calculates 10-year risk of coronary events based on age, total cholesterol, HDL) Tj T* (cholesterol, systolic blood pressure, smoking status, and diabetes. While effective for primary prevention epidemiology, Framingham relies strictly) Tj T* (on static regression coefficients and lacks non-invasive stress testing attributes \(e.g., exercise ST depression, nuclear scintigraphy\).) Tj  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 8 Tf (The Diamond-Forrester Model:) Tj /F1 8 Tf ( Widely used in cardiology clinics to estimate pre-test probability of angiographically significant CAD based on) Tj T* (age, biological sex, and chest pain symptom classification \(typical, atypical, non-anginal\). However, Diamond-Forrester frequently overestimates) Tj T* (disease likelihood in female patients and fails to incorporate dynamic treadmill performance biomarkers.) Tj  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 8 Tf (ACC/AHA and ESC Clinical Guidelines:) Tj /F1 8 Tf ( Modern European Society of Cardiology \(ESC\) and American College of Cardiology \(ACC\) guidelines) Tj T* (recommend multi-modality integration. By uniting demographic factors with resting ECG, treadmill exercise metrics \(`thalach`, `oldpeak`, `slope`\),) Tj T* (fluoroscopy calcification \(`ca`\), and perfusion scintigraphy \(`thal`\), our MLOps platform achieves a far richer, multidimensional prognostic) Tj T* (evaluation.) Tj T* ET
