BT 1 0 0 1 0 49.5 Tm 11.5 TL /F1 8 Tf .176471 .215686 .282353 rg (The original Cleveland database recorded coronary disease on an ordinal integer scale from `0` to `4`: `0` denotes total absence of coronary) Tj T* (narrowing \() Tj (< 50% luminal reduction\), while `{1, 2, 3, 4}` denote angiographically confirmed stenosis >= 50% in 1, 2, 3, or 4 major coronary arteries.) Tj T* (In clinical cardiology, any patient with >= 50% stenosis in a major vessel has established coronary artery disease requiring intensive medical) Tj T* (therapy. Consequently, we mapped: `target = 0` if raw diagnosis = 0 \(Absence, N=164, 54.13%\) and `target = 1` if raw diagnosis in {1, 2, 3, 4}) Tj T* (\(Presence, N=139, 45.87%\). This yields a well-balanced clinical classification problem with 303 total patient records.) Tj T* ET
